  "summary": "While neighboring Arizona cities including Tempe, Chandler, Cave Creek and Surprise have canceled their Flock ALPR contracts, Scottsdale continues to operate its 85 Flock cameras under a $370,000/year contract. Council members say an ordinance and auditor review are being prepared before a public council discussion, though some councilmembers and candidates have called for ending the contract.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "My top priority is to end Scottsdale's contract with Flock",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "We're currently working with City Manager Caton and Police Chief LeDuc to get the (Flock) auditor review, usage data, and the proposed ordinance in hand before council creates policy",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "Scottsdale evaluates this technology based on our own experience, policies, safeguards and public safety needs",
      "paragraph_idx": 27
    },
    {
      "quote": "Eleven Arizona communities have already rejected Flock, understanding that a Flock contract is a gateway",
      "paragraph_idx": 38
    }
  ],
